ok    Test boot           a test VM booted and ran a program in 1.1 s
ok    Disk space          120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
warn  Disk encryption     data drive NOT encrypted; swap /dev/dm-1 encrypted (LUKS2)
      note: The drive is not encrypted. Puddle keeps secrets in memory while it runs (the real
            values behind the stand-ins a workspace holds), and memory can be paged out to swap
            or written to disk in a crash dump. On a drive that is not encrypted, anyone who
            gets the disk (a lost or stolen computer, a disk taken out) can read those pages and
            the data folder; on an encrypted one they cannot. Put the drive under LUKS (the
            installer's "encrypt the disk" option; an existing drive needs a backup and a
            reinstall or `cryptsetup reencrypt`). For swap alone, give it a random key each
            boot: in /etc/crypttab, `swap /dev/<swap partition> /dev/urandom
            swap,cipher=aes-xts-plain64,size=512`, and use /dev/mapper/swap in /etc/fstab; or
            turn swap off with `sudo swapoff -a` if the machine has the memory.
ok    SSH agent           the agent on /run/user/1000/agent.sock holds 1 key (ed25519: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)      version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store    the operating system's credential store: a test write and delete worked

